    },
    {
      "id": "Hd44TJF57kjAVd9Gl4Roi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1152.9733471840045,
      "y": -1759.5267110453692,
      "width": 2881.845703125,
      "height": 2439.022988505746,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 83380586,
      "version": 329,
      "versionNonce": 1849107921,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776085372074,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Mint Token:\n\n      1) Miner submits hashrate proof and legal document URI.\n\n      2) Protocol mints an NFT (legal proof) to the miner’s account (protocol as authority).\n\n      3) Simultaneously mints proportional BHRT tokens representing the miner’s hashrate.\n\n      4) Ensures token issuance matches committed mining power.\n\n\nAMM BHRT/USDC:\n\n      1) Provides a decentralized liquidity pool for swapping BHRT tokens against USDC.\n\n      2) Enables miners, protocol, and investors to buy/sell BHRT at market-driven prices.\n\n      3) Uses constant product formula (x * y = k) for automatic price discovery and liquidity.\n\n\nRevoke Hashrate Stake:\n\n      1) Miner deposits BHRT tokens back to protocol signifying exit intention.\n\n      2) Protocol burns the miner’s NFT, formally revoking their legal claim to mining power.\n\n      3) Returns mining power rights to the miner off-chain (or updates state).\n\n      4) BHRT tokens are burned to reduce circulating supply accordingly.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 62.94252873563215,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Mint Token:\n\n      1) Miner submits hashrate proof and legal document URI.\n\n      2) Protocol mints an NFT (legal proof) to the miner’s account (protocol as authority).\n\n      3) Simultaneously mints proportional BHRT tokens representing the miner’s hashrate.\n\n      4) Ensures token issuance matches committed mining power.\n\n\nAMM BHRT/USDC:\n\n      1) Provides a decentralized liquidity pool for swapping BHRT tokens against USDC.\n\n      2) Enables miners, protocol, and investors to buy/sell BHRT at market-driven prices.\n\n      3) Uses constant product formula (x * y = k) for automatic price discovery and liquidity.\n\n\nRevoke Hashrate Stake:\n\n      1) Miner deposits BHRT tokens back to protocol signifying exit intention.\n\n      2) Protocol burns the miner’s NFT, formally revoking their legal claim to mining power.\n\n      3) Returns mining power rights to the miner off-chain (or updates state).\n\n      4) BHRT tokens are burned to reduce circulating supply accordingly.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HX40frO7qRAjQOxhW5QI0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -7640.359986149328,
      "y": -1556.1933777120353,
      "width": 2882.44970703125,
      "height": 2560.344827586213,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 54376566,
      "version": 607,
      "versionNonce": 278109119,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776085372074,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Stake:\n\n       1) User deposits BHRT tokens into the vault as collateral.\n\n       2) Vault reads the live BHRT USD value via oracle to calculate collateral worth.\n\n       3) User mints HST stablecoins up to a safe collateral ratio (e.g., 150%).\n\n       4) Records user’s collateral and debt position on-chain for tracking.\n\nLiquidation:\n\n       1) Protocol monitors collateral ratios using oracle prices.\n\n       2) If a vault’s collateral falls below the liquidation threshold, anyone\n           (a liquidator) can repay part/all of the stablecoin debt.\n\n       3) Liquidator receives seized BHRT collateral (often at a discount as incentive).\n\n       4) Updates vault state to maintain system solvency and peg stability.\n\nDebt Settlement:\n\n       1) User repays (burns) HST stablecoins to reduce or clear their debt.\n\n       2) Vault verifies repayment and collateral sufficiency via oracle price checks.\n\n       3) Upon full repayment, user withdraws their BHRT collateral tokens.\n\n       4) Vault updates records to reflect closed or reduced positions.",
      "fontSize": 68.27586206896567,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Stake:\n\n       1) User deposits BHRT tokens into the vault as collateral.\n\n       2) Vault reads the live BHRT USD value via oracle to calculate collateral worth.\n\n       3) User mints HST stablecoins up to a safe collateral ratio (e.g., 150%).\n\n       4) Records user’s collateral and debt position on-chain for tracking.\n\nLiquidation:\n\n       1) Protocol monitors collateral ratios using oracle prices.\n\n       2) If a vault’s collateral falls below the liquidation threshold, anyone\n           (a liquidator) can repay part/all of the stablecoin debt.\n\n       3) Liquidator receives seized BHRT collateral (often at a discount as incentive).\n\n       4) Updates vault state to maintain system solvency and peg stability.\n\nDebt Settlement:\n\n       1) User repays (burns) HST stablecoins to reduce or clear their debt.\n\n       2) Vault verifies repayment and collateral sufficiency via oracle price checks.\n\n       3) Upon full repayment, user withdraws their BHRT collateral tokens.\n\n       4) Vault updates records to reflect closed or reduced positions.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
